<p>President Trump removed US Attorney General Pam Bondi on April 2 and named Deputy Attorney General Todd Blanche to lead the Justice Department on an acting basis. The move ends Bondi’s roughly year-long tenure atop the department. Across multiple reports, the most frequently cited reason was growing dissatisfaction with Bondi’s handling of files related to Jeffrey Epstein, an issue that drew criticism and political pressure around the administration. Several outlets also reported that President Trump had grown frustrated with Bondi’s broader performance, including her pace in pursuing cases against figures he wanted investigated or prosecuted. Trump said Bondi would move to a private-sector role while Blanche runs the department on an interim basis.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/69PD4idw1yw-p4SCVUcP8y-tBRb9xIkWyzKrGIDGtRjngHjRwR2WgzYhTQjK5IC4hH3e_7AN1cZ69fEXwyc6u13ofFbNIhRsbdEHb1u4UzxlF4_KytqKuVHxiFlmq2-orNwYF1zQAmk1dY6NPxrrnj_IVQ1r0Gm0Jahx3NPM9w99thN6FeEPvvPEKmQmqSYhU3FATfjzVMTERyVF4bInKE0MXuC8O0OyYTfYy6S1m0Jb7jD4n3D3M-1h8Nh2BiJ78EuXLv4SK21nqtHrbw' alt='Pam Bondi at a Senate Judiciary Committee hearing on oversight of the Department of Justice, on Capitol Hill, Oct. 7, 2025.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Blanche profile: Acting attorney general Todd Blanche previously served as a federal prosecutor and later represented Trump in the criminal hush-money case before becoming deputy attorney general.</li><li>Justice norms: Several reports said Bondi’s tenure was marked by moves that weakened the Justice Department’s traditional independence from the White House in its investigative work.</li><li>Cross-party backlash: Reports said Bondi faced criticism over the Epstein files from both Democrats and Republicans, including Trump allies and some GOP lawmakers.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President Trump: Trump praised Bondi publicly as a &quot;Great American Patriot&quot; and a loyal friend, while announcing that she would move to a private-sector job and that Todd Blanche would take over on an acting basis. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/trump-fires-pam-bondi-as-us-attorney-general-white-house-official/article70817192.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Pam Bondi: Bondi said leading Trump’s public-safety agenda had been &quot;the honor of a lifetime&quot; before leaving for a private-sector role. (<a href='https://www.rt.com/news/637105-trump-fired-pam-bondi/'>RT</a>)</li><li>White House critics: Critics of Bondi focused on the Epstein files, accusing her of mismanaging the issue and turning it into a political liability for the administration. (<a href='https://www.ft.com/content/533ecec7-713f-46f1-a2a2-cbd9a659299f'>Financial Times</a>)</li><li>Media analysts: Some coverage linked Bondi’s removal to a broader pileup of political problems for the White House, rather than treating it as only a Justice Department personnel change. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/united-states-canada/article/3348858/trump-fires-pam-bondi-us-attorney-general-amid-epstein-files-furore'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/4/3/donald-trump-fires-loyalist-attorney-general-pam-bondi'>Donald Trump fires loyalist Attorney General Pam Bondi</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/533ecec7-713f-46f1-a2a2-cbd9a659299f'>Trump fires US attorney-general Pam Bondi</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/united-states-canada/article/3348858/trump-fires-pam-bondi-us-attorney-general-amid-epstein-files-furore'>Trump fires Pam Bondi as US president’s frustration with bad news, top officials grows</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/ce843ge47z4o'>Trump removes US Attorney General Pam Bondi</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/apr/02/trump-white-house-ballroom-republicans-dhs-funding-deal-tariffs-latest-news-updates'>Trum